      "content": "That's a good start on the core concepts, but to be honest, the length is a bit low for what the digital library is looking for. It's actually quite short if we're looking at the character count metric. \n\nCan you expand on this significantly? I want you to go into much more detail regarding the mathematical derivation using wave packets and perhaps the implications for the observer effect vs the intrinsic uncertainty. \n\nAgain, please keep it useful for the students—I'm looking for depth and technical rigor, not just fluff. If I see the same sentence repeated or just a bunch of empty adjectives, I won't be able to use it. Can you give me a much lengthier, more exhaustive version?",
